Tested `UserProfileLoader`, which had none. It is the component every other piece of the user menu depends on — the avatar, the display name and the "My profile" entry all read the store it fills — so an unnoticed fault in it looks like three separate bugs in three separate components, which is exactly how it presented. The tests cover the cases that matter: nobody signed in, a user already held, a request in flight, a different user signing in, a cold store where nothing is initialised, and a refusal that must not become a request per render. @ericof
